# macOS
.DS_Store

# Office lock files
~$*.xlsx

# Distillation exports (personal data — never commit)
written-distillation-*.csv
# The term-labelling sheet: one person's whole music library in plain text,
# the same class as an export and equally unwelcome in history.
ontology-terms.csv
# The Calendar review artefact: event titles, locations and organiser names —
# other people's, not only the owner's, which is the trade `CalendarDistiller`
# makes deliberately and the reason the vault never returns them. §10 forbids
# raw Calendar payloads in logs and traces; a file in the working tree is not
# either of those, and it is not something to commit.
calendar-review-*.md

# Credentials. None of these belong in a repository, and the reason this list
# exists rather than trusting care is that an APNs key was committed by a
# `git add -A` within a minute of being downloaded — caught only because it was
# still unpushed. A `.p8` sends notifications to every install of the app; an
# App Store Connect `.p8` uploads builds as you; `sb_secret_…` bypasses RLS
# entirely. Downloads default to the folder you happen to be in, which on this
# machine is this one.
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
AuthKey_*
.env
.env.*
# …but `semantic/.env.example` holds no secret and must be committed: it is what
# documents `DATABASE_URL`, `WORKER_ID` and `CALENDAR_LINEAGE_HMAC_KEY` for the
# worker. Without this line `git add -A` skips it silently, which is the same
# quiet-omission failure the rules above exist to prevent.
!semantic/.env.example

# Xcode user state
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
DerivedData/
build/

# Regenerable harness output — screenshots and overlays, half a megabyte a round.
tools/out/
# Where `run_layout_audit.sh` actually writes: accessibility dumps and
# `.xcresult` bundles, tens of thousands of files a run. The line above covers a
# path the script does not use.
out/

# The ingestion Lambda builds locally; neither the tree nor the zip belongs in git.
aws/ingestion/node_modules/
aws/ingestion/dist/
aws/worker/dist/
aws/classifier/dist/

# Python bytecode from running the semantic tests and tools.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Wrangler's local cache, created by `npx wrangler deploy`. Holds
# `wrangler-account.json`, which carries the Cloudflare account id — a local
# working file rather than anything the repository should describe.
.wrangler/
